UID:9e405ca5b08995c6bdc3ca2017d86a12@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,reading
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nJoin us for a unique dance and martial
  arts experience! Capoeira (pronounced kaa-puh-weh-ruh) is an Afro-Brazili
 an art form that blends dance\, music\, acrobatics\, and tradition. To the
  sounds of the berimbau\, atabaque\, pandeiro\, and more\, we will learn t
 he ginga\, traditional rhythms\, and clever techniques rooted in resistanc
 e and cultural expression. All levels are welcome - come move\, play\, and
  connect! Presented by Chicago Capoeira Center and Centro Cultural Quilomb
 o\, a nonprofit cultural organ\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocom
 mons.com/events/6ac53e04901b02002cc08038
LOCATION:Sulzer Regional\, 4455 N. Lincoln Ave.\, Chicago\, IL 60625
URL:https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/events/6ac53e04901b02002cc08038
