DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nWalter Henri Dyett\, known as “Capta
 in Dyett”\, was a music educator\, and instrumental figure in the develo
 pment of jazz and black music in Chicago. As the band instructor of Bronze
 ville’s DuSable High School\, Dyett built a powerhouse music program tha
 t produced iconic singers such as Nat King Cole\, Dinah Washington\, Ella 
 Jenkins\, and Johnny Hartman. His program also produced many great instrum
 entalists including Richard Davis\, Dorothy Donegan\, Muhal Richard Abrams
 \, Julian Priester\, Joseph Jarman\,\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bib
 liocommons.com/events/6a6cc513cca66c2f00a74fd2
