BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tlingit Artist James Johnson: Haa Shagoon—The Path Forward
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261110T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261110T190000
DTSTAMP:20261107T144344Z
UID:a1bf775c6eedc59be03426f8e9f5d56d@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nAs part of Native American He
 ritage Month \, join us for an evening conversation with James Johnson. Ja
 mes will discuss his artistic practice\, the importance of preserving trad
 itional Tlingit ways of creating\, and how he draws on the knowledge and w
 ork of his ancestors in his contemporary practice. James Johnson is an awa
 rd-winning Tlingit Artist and Carver\, born and raised in Juneau\, AK. He 
 belongs to the Tlingit Ch’áak’ Dakl’aweidi Clan (Eagle Killerwhale)
 . James is a multi-disciplinary artist but specializes in Tlingit formline
  design\, with a focus on traditional wood carving. Carving is an integral
  part of the preservation of Tlingit history and culture. “Carving is ou
 r visual language that represents who the Tlingit people are\, and how we 
 live in balance with all things.” James’s contemporary practice builds
  upon an indigenous artistic continuum while honoring the culture and its 
 rich traditions. This event takes place on a Legendary Late Hours day and 
 is included with admission. The event takes place in the Montgomery Ward L
 ecture Hall\, on the lower level.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.
 org/our-events/cultural-programming/tlingit-artist-james-johnson-haa-shago
 onthe-path-forward
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/cultural-programming/tlingit-ar
 tist-james-johnson-haa-shagoonthe-path-forward
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Tlingit Artist James Johnson: Haa Shagoon—The Path
  Forward
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: Tlingit Artist James Johnson: Haa Shagoon—The Pa
 th Forward
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
