UID:f9f829d67051c6fe3c3cad8e955823dd@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,reading
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nJoin us for a Native American Heritage Mon
 th screening of Hunting in Wartime . Hunting in Wartime profiles Tlingit v
 eterans from Hoonah\, Alaska who saw combat during the Vietnam War. The ve
 terans talk about surviving trauma\, relating to Vietnamese communities\, 
 readjusting to civilian life\, and serving a government that systematicall
 y oppresses native people. Their stories give an important human face to t
 he combat soldier and show the lasting affects of war on individuals\, fam
 ilies and communiti\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/ev
 ents/6ac6b387ebad22004543cfdb
LOCATION:Lozano\, 1805 S. Loomis St.\, Chicago\, IL 60608
URL:https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/events/6ac6b387ebad22004543cfdb
